                <pb facs="0405" n="281" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg281"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">824.00/170: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Bolivia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Maginnis</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-01-27T17:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 27,
                                1921—5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>3. Your January 25, 10 p.m.</p>
                <p>Cable Department whether, in your opinion, disturbances are likely to occur which
                    would prove embarrassing to the United States if the Government of Bolivia were
                    accorded formal recognition after the inauguration of Saavedra. Will the
                    convention continue to function as a congress for the constitutional period, or
                    will new general elections be held next May?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Colby</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
